@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: CHANGELOG.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Every figure below names the model it was measured on, because quality where a model is involved is a property of that model and not of this code." }
~ Every figure in the changelog names the model it was measured on.

To ensure clarity about the quality of measurements, which is a property of the model used.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:9e883b906b45c1d82062f44f9cd0fca675830cc7 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "They cost real time, and a release note that hides them invites someone to spend it again." }
~ Rejected experiments are listed beside shipped ones in the changelog.

To document what did not work and why, to prevent others from repeating unnecessary experiments.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "What did work: **two-pass agreement** (170 and 192 flags became 96, and it removed every false flag on a real commit in development), which is why `check` runs two passes by default." }
~ The `check` command runs two passes by default.

To improve the precision of findings without incurring excessive costs.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: CHANGELOG.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The tool assigns every label, source and status; a model proposes content only." }
~ The tool assigns labels, sources, and statuses; a model proposes content only.

To ensure that the tool's output is reliable and verifiable.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: CHANGELOG.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Every quote is checked against the commit, and an absent quote caps its unit at `speculative`." }
~ Every quote is checked against the commit it came from.

To ensure that quotes are accurate and relevant to the code being analyzed.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "What the code says about itself never verifies it. Doc comments, string literals and commit subjects are marked as prose: they help find the right code and never establish a claim." }
~ What the code says about itself never verifies it.

To prevent self-referential claims from being treated as verified facts.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A single run never raises a status. `Supported` needs every part of a claim covered by structural facts *and* two independent runs agreeing, or a person's word." }
~ A single run never raises a status.

To ensure that claims are supported by multiple independent runs or human review before being considered verified.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A test linked to a claim waits for a person. A model proposing the link is not a review; a failing test never backs anything. }
~ A test linked to a claim waits for a person.

To ensure that tests are reviewed and verified by humans before being considered evidence.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Review is recorded, never a rewrite. Confirming writes an attestation, rejecting a withdrawal with a reason, closing a resolution with a note. Nothing is deleted." }
~ Review is recorded, never a rewrite.

To maintain an immutable record of decisions and reviews, ensuring transparency and accountability.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: README.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Nothing is hidden. A prompt that had to be cut, an answer that had to be salvaged, a set of units split across calls, a provider that truncated — each is reported where it happened." }
~ Nothing is hidden in the tool's output.

To provide complete transparency about the processes and decisions made by the tool.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: CHANGELOG.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The default build has no TLS stack and speaks plain HTTP to a model on your machine; `--features hosted` is the opt-in for a hosted provider. }
~ The default build has no TLS stack and speaks plain HTTP to a model on your machine.

To provide a lightweight and secure default configuration for users who do not require a hosted provider.

@decision d/g9e883b906b45-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: CHANGELOG.md@9e883b906b45 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": MSRV 1.86 for the shipped crates. }
~ MSRV 1.86 for the shipped crates.

To ensure compatibility with a wide range of Rust versions while maintaining modern features and performance improvements.

